{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Done. pyknotid 0.5.3 is built from source, patched for NumPy 2.x / Python 3.13, and installed into the global env, with all compiled Cython extensions working.\n\n## What the environment was missing\nPython 3.13.7 / NumPy 2.3.0 / gcc 12.2 were present, but no `setuptools`, `Cython`, or runtime deps. Installed them (`setuptools`, `wheel`, `cython`, `sympy`, `networkx`, `planarity`, `peewee`, `vispy`, `appdirs`, `requests`, `tqdm`) before building.\n\n## Build\nCloned to `/app/pyknotid` as instructed, then `python3 setup.py build_ext --inplace` compiled all four Cython extensions (chelpers, ccomplexity, coctree, cinvariants). Built extension modules are `.so` files in both the source tree and site-packages.\n\n## Compatibility fixes (all read from the actual errors)\nNumPy 2 removals (`np.int`, `np.float`, `np.complex` no longer exist):\n- `np.int` → `np.int64` across `knot.py`, `openknot.py`, `periodiccell.py`, `representations/representation.py`, `representations/dtnotation.py`, and the three `np.zeros(..., dtype=np.int)` in `spacecurves/ccomplexity.pyx`\n- `np.float` → `np.float64` in `spacecurve.py`, `make/periodic_knot.py`\n- `n.complex`/`n.float` → `n.complex128`/`n.float64` and builtin `complex` in `invariants.py`\n(`np.bool` is still valid in NumPy 2.x, so left alone.)\n\nPython 3.13 removals:\n- `from fractions import gcd` → `from math import gcd` in `make/torus.py`\n\nVersion-API drift:\n- `planarity` renamed drawplanar attributes (`pos`/`start`/`end` → `vertex_position`/`edge_position`/...). Added `_drawplanar_attr` in `representation.py` accepting either naming, fixing `test_reconstructed_space_curve`.\n- Stale absolute imports `from coctree import ...` (`simplify/octree.py`) and `from periodiccell import ...` (`spacecurves/periodic.py`) → full package paths.\n\n## Verification (run against the installed copy)\n- README snippet from the task returns `6.999999999999998` (README shows ~7.0), no errors.\n- Extensions load as C extensions and execute in their original context: `chelpers.find_crossings`, `ccomplexity.cython_second_order_writhes`/`cython_higher_order_writhe`, `cinvariants.vassiliev_degree_3`, `coctree.angle_exceeds`. The full README example (`alexander_polynomial(t)` via sympy, `vassiliev_degree_3`, `octree_simplify`) also runs.\n- Test suite: `18 passed`, ignoring `test_random_curves.py` (imports the nonexistent `pyknotid.make.randomwalks`, dead code) and `test_catalogue.py` (needs a downloaded knots database).\n\nOn the other pre-existing dead files, for transparency: `pyknotid/spacecurves/periodicline.py` has a syntax error in upstream 0.5.3 (`class PeriodicKnot` with no colon/body); it is referenced nowhere and I left it untouched since \"fixing\" it would mean inventing a body. Everything else imports cleanly."}}
